        "raw": "<p>So I was playing in the Temple of Zhu long, and the Villain wiped all three Shinobi Assassins. \"Aha,\" thought I, \"to keep that from happening again, I'll pile them all on The Wraith's deck and then play this Impromptu Invention, so I only have to deal with ONE Assassin from the draw and the rest get buried in her deck.\"</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I do that, and when I play the Invention, I get:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\"The Wraith would draw Shinobi Assassin, so Shinobi Assassin is put into play!\"</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\"The Wraith would draw Shinobi Assassin, so Shinobi Assassin is put into play!\"</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\"The Wraith would draw Shinobi Assassin, so Shinobi Assassin is put into play!\"</p>\r\n\r\n<p>...and then The Wraith drew the top card of her deck (I think) and searched for an equipment.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For a bit, I thought searching through the deck might have been revealing the Assassins, but later on I was successfully able to bury them all in the Idealist's deck after a search with Conceptualize.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>There was something else that game where what should have been a single card draw caused a multiple-Assassin chain, but I don't remember what it was.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Assassins are weird!</p>",
