        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": "",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Aha, I just found this buried in the Fireside Chat thread:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\"When Shinobi Assassin is on top of a hero deck, it does not prevent the draw, discard, reveal, or play actions. When it is interacted with, it takes effect and enters play, but the original action continues with the top hero card. For example, if you draw a card, the Shinobi Assassin enters play, and then you draw the top card.\"</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I didn't expect that at all, but okay! Ninjas are unexpected. I'll have to factor that into my plans now.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In looking for this on the wiki, I noticed there are no clarifications for the Temple of Zhu long (nor in the big roll-up, because that pulls from individual pages). Looks like we need to do some fixing...</p>",
